    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d539">

                <pb facs="0530" n="454" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.00/527</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Secretary of the Navy
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 14, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your letter of the 9th of February, informing the Department of the
                    proposed withdrawal of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Chester</hi> from
                    Liberian waters, and in reply <pb facs="0531" n="455" xml:id="pg455"/> to say
                    that a telegram has been received from the American Minister at Monrovia
                    recommending, with the concurrence of the commander of the vessel, that its
                    station at Monrovia be continued at least two weeks after the arrival of the
                    arms and ammunition which the Government of Liberia has recently purchased in
                    this country.</p>
                <p>Great good has been accomplished by the presence of the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Chester</hi> in West African waters in preventing a more
                    extended uprising of native tribes which so seriously threatened the Republic,
                    and I take this occasion to express the Department’s deep appreciation of the
                    valuable assistance rendered by your Department in causing the vessel to be put
                    to that useful service.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
